  "prompt_text": "The figure is a schematic of a three-dimensional cellular or polyhedral network, showing how geometric quantities are assigned to different parts of the structure. Several adjacent cells are drawn as translucent polyhedra sharing faces, edges, and vertices. One central face is highlighted in darker green to indicate a face labeled with an area term, while a small orange patch on that face represents a stress or tension-like quantity acting within the face. Red arrows point inward on this patch, suggesting in-plane forces associated with the face.\n\nThe diagram also marks a shared edge with a length label and highlights it with yellow arrows, implying a line-based quantity along that edge. A black dot at a corner is identified as a vertex, and a green arrow nearby indicates a force vector associated with that vertex. Lower in the figure, one whole cell is labeled with a volume term, and a small blue cube inside it is annotated with blue arrows pointing inward from different directions, indicating a pressure-like quantity within the cell.\n\nOverall, the image explains a mechanical description of a tessellated tissue or foam-like material in terms of cell volumes, face areas, edge lengths, vertex forces, face tensions, and cell pressures.",
